# Unselected Windows native pathname primitives for the existing tool adapter.
# No new C struct/layout or language grammar: reparse bytes are the documented
# FSCTL_GET_REPARSE_POINT result on the Windows ULONG4/USHORT2/WCHAR2 LE ABI.
# ntifs.h4394-4418 is the format reference, not a kernel-mode include dependency.
# Native query results keep their OS error before cleanup.
# 0 success,1 OS error,-1 allocation/encoding; readlink2 unsupported reparse tag.
# Non-strict scalar UTF-8 port of CPython3.14 ntpath.py join/split/normpath
# and realpath(strict=False). Changes: owned heap strings/vectors instead of
# Python objects; counted native queries and explicit OS/internal outcomes.
# join uses Unicode16 full lower; deep-link seen keys use native normcase.
# This adapter does not claim Python's lone-surrogate pathname domain.
# Copyright (c) 2001 Python Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved.
#
